/ActualText (Built a self-hostable, multi-algorithm rate limiting service in Rust using Axum, supporting fixed window, sliding window, and token bucket strategies for API traffic control\nImplemented atomic request-counting logic via Redis Lua scripting to prevent race conditions under concurrent load\nDesigned a multi-tenant architecture with per-client API keys, enabling usage-based access control similar to Upstash Ratelimit\nExposed a simple REST API \(POST /v1/limit\) returning real-time allow/deny decisions with remaining quota and reset timestamps)
